tips-dataset-52 = As a Salvage Specialist, consider cooperating with the Supply Specialists. They can order a wide variety of useful items, including laser guns and shuttle-building materials.
tips-dataset-53 = As a Supply Specialist, consider asking R&D for a Ripley APLU. With a hydraulic clamp, it can move fuel tanks and deliveries efficiently.
tips-dataset-54 = As a Supply Specialist, maintain a surplus of materials for scientists and public works crews.
tips-dataset-55 = As a Supply Specialist, keep enough operating cash available before risking any surplus on gambling.
tips-dataset-56 = As a Supply Specialist, remember that emergency requisitions can provide vital defensive equipment.

nf-tips-dataset-93 = Each ID card can have a shuttle attached to it. Ask the Superintendent for another ID if you need to purchase an additional shuttle.
nf-tips-dataset-94 = The Superintendent can rename your shuttle. Usually it is enough to hand over your ID and ask.
nf-tips-dataset-106 = The CWO has access to long-range radar. Outlaws should watch for Prowlers in the void.
nf-tips-dataset-110 = Your PDA includes a bounty application. If you fulfill a posted bounty, ask the Superintendent or Warden about a reward.
nf-tips-dataset-112 = Keep your IFF enabled unless you intend to hide, or a CWO patrol may investigate your ship.
nf-tips-dataset-114 = Expeditions can yield rare and illegal items. Do not leave contraband lying around if you want to avoid a CWO boarding.

ghost-role-information-clippy-description = The Superintendent’s loyal worker, smelling faintly of cardboard and paper.
